                <pb facs="0851" n="815" xml:id="pg815"/>

                <head>346. Memorandum of Conversation<anchor n="0" xml:id="d346-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">MCT MC/9</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian"
                            type="conversation-or-meeting-date" when="1958-06-09T16:00:00">June 9,
                            1958, 4 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">MACMILLAN TALKS</p>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Anglo-American Relations with General de Gaulle’s Government</item>
                </list>
                <p>[Here follows the same list of participants as <ref target="#d344">Document
                        344</ref>.]</p>
                <p>The Secretary raised the question of what general policy the US and UK should
                    adopt vis-à-vis General de Gaulle and his Government. [3–1/2 <hi
                        rendition="#italic">lines of source text not declassified</hi>] The
                    President believed that we should specify subjects where we want General de
                    Gaulle’s participation and perhaps take the initiative in asking him in. [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">2 lines of source text not declassified</hi>] He cited
                    the Summit preparations and NATO problems as examples of questions in which
                    General de Gaulle should be brought in.</p>
                <p>[Here follows further discussion of this subject.]</p>
                <p>[<hi rendition="#italic">1½ lines of source text not declassified</hi>] the
                    Secretary agreed, and summarized the consensus on this subject as follows:</p>
                <p>We would undertake a tripartite relationship with de Gaulle in those areas where
                    there exist an historical basis for it, such as in the Summit preparations and
                    the re-unification of Germany. Otherwise, we will deal with the French through
                    bilateral arrangements and, when appropriate, through NATO. [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">2 lines of source text not declassified</hi>]</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
